[{"sha":"c8dbf96e9dfee43b30f7c3f440175d6bd4de61de","node_id":"C_kwDOLeedi9oAKGM4ZGJmOTZlOWRmZWU0M2IzMGY3YzNmNDQwMTc1ZDZiZDRkZTYxZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tanishq","email":"slatorgator3@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-03T13:53:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"Harry","email":"harry0703@hotmail.com","date":"2026-11-04T02:11:21Z"},"message":"fix(video): stop keys typed into the console window from cutting the video short or stalling the clip join\n\nThe FFmpeg that joins the clips of every video ran without -nostdin, so\nit read keys from the console it inherits: the webui.bat window, or the\nconsole of main.py or cli.py. A \"q\" typed there stops the join with exit\ncode 0, and the task finishes with a video whose footage ends at that\npoint, followed by a black frame with subtitles for the rest of the\nnarration. A \"c\" opens FFmpeg's \"Enter command\" prompt, and the join\nthen waits for Enter until ffmpeg_concat_timeout_seconds (3600 s by\ndefault) fails the task. On Windows, a key typed into the window while\nnothing reads it, even before the task starts, waits there and is read\nwhen the join starts.\n\nThe other FFmpeg commands in app/ that process media (voice.py, bgm.py,\nmaterial_upload.py, sonilo.py, elevenlabs_music.py, video_project.py)\nalready pass -nostdin, and MoviePy starts its FFmpeg processes with\nstdin set to DEVNULL or a pipe.","tree":{"sha":"b184a92605cf9e52829ffca7ab9b56f98ab2cac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harry0703/MoneyPrinterTurbo/git/trees/b184a92605cf9e52829ffca7ab9b56f98ab2cac5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harry0703/MoneyPrinterTurbo/git/commits/c8dbf96e9dfee43b30f7c3f440175d6bd4de61de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harry0703/MoneyPrinterTurbo/commits/c8dbf96e9dfee43b30f7c3f440175d6bd4de61de","html_url":"https://github.com/harry0703/MoneyPrinterTurbo/commit/c8dbf96e9dfee43b30f7c3f440175d6bd4de61